## Error Handling

All API errors extend `ApiError`. The exception hierarchy is:

- `ApiError` (base)
  - `ClientError` (4xx)
    - `BadRequestError` (400)
    - `UnauthorizedError` (401)
    - `ForbiddenError` (403)
    - `NotFoundError` (404)
    - `ConflictError` (409)
    - `UnprocessableEntityError` (422)
  - `ServerError` (5xx)
    - `InternalServerError` (500)

```php
use {{invokerPackage}}\Errors\NotFoundError;
use {{invokerPackage}}\Errors\ClientError;
use {{invokerPackage}}\Errors\ServerError;
use {{invokerPackage}}\Errors\ApiError;

try {
    $result = $client->petApi->getPetById($petId);
} catch (NotFoundError $e) {
    echo "Not found: " . $e->getMessage();
} catch (ClientError $e) {
    echo "Client error " . $e->getStatusCode() . ": " . $e->getMessage();
} catch (ServerError $e) {
    echo "Server error: " . $e->getMessage();
} catch (ApiError $e) {
    echo "API error: " . $e->getMessage();
}
```

## Configuration

### Custom Transport Options

```php
use {{invokerPackage}}\TransportOptions;

$transport = TransportOptions::builder()
    ->proxy('http://proxy:3128')
    ->timeout(5000)
    ->build();

$client = new {{clientClassName}}($authenticator, $transport);
```

## API Methods

Each API group is exposed as a typed property on the client (e.g., `$client->petApi`). API classes have methods that correspond to OpenAPI operations, accepting typed request parameters and returning typed response models.

## Models

Models are generated as PHP classes under the `{{invokerPackage}}\Models` namespace.

```php
use {{invokerPackage}}\Models\Pet;

$pet = new Pet(name: 'Fido', status: 'available');
```

## Binary / File Uploads

File upload parameters accept `SplFileInfo` or file path strings. Binary response bodies are returned as `string`.

## Comment Style

Never use inline comments (`//`). Always use block comments (`/* ... */`). PHPDoc `/** ... */` is fine.

```good
/* This explains the logic */
$x = 1;
```

```bad
// This explains the logic
$x = 1;
```
